  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy guidelines on synthetic science</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Synthetic biology or engineering biology is a fast-moving field that embraces and drives state-of-the-art technologies for designing and reconstructing livings systems at different scales, primarily by reprogramming cellular genetic information. engineering biology raises a number of policy issues around R&amp;D funding, Public Private Partnership, infrastructure requirements, education and training, intellectual property, regulation, and public engagement. One of the issues that need to be addressed is how engineering biology in general is taught at universities and higher education institutes in the Asia Pacific region and what are the guidelines for formulating such curriculum</narrative>
  </description>
